chapter AFP

session HOL_in_HOL_Deep = HOL +
  description "A locally-nameless deep embedding of classical higher-order logic (Church's simple theory of types) after Benzmueller, Brown and Kohlhase: the calculus NK is proved sound, Henkin-complete and consistent, entirely within plain Isabelle/HOL. Completeness is strengthened to open formulas, arbitrary infinite carriers and signatures, and derivation from hypotheses; Cantor's theorem is derived inside the calculus, and compactness yields consistency with a scheme of inequations between new individual constants without constructing an infinite model; the Dedekind axiom of infinity derives every constant-free sentence 'there are at least n individuals', and neither the scheme nor these sentences derive the axiom. Targets Isabelle2025-2."
  options [timeout = 600]
  sessions
    "HOL-Library"
    "HOL-Eisbach"
  theories
    Syntax
    Semantics
    Calculus
    Soundness
    Completeness
    Consistency
    NK_Infinity
    Cantor
    Main_Results
    Footprint_Checks
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
